At Basic you can only use them with the rook move from chess.
Straight ahead.  That means they are only usefull at the doors
to the two castles and you remain exposed to wand shots.  Get
to Skilled and you can use them with the knight move from chess
and are much less subject to wand shots.  It is very questionable
if it is worth using unless you get plenty of XP slots.

On the weight issue - I've taken up ignoring almost any polearm
but spetum because of weight.  If my character can get to Skilled
in polearm (not a tourist) I might use the first polearm I find and
every time I find one check the weight and drop the heavier one
until I end up with a spetum.  If my character can only reach
Basic that strategy ends up meaning the spetum is in my near-by
stash not even in the bag.



